<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- THE BAKED ROOT. This is what makes the environment a property of the
	     BITS rather than of whatever shell happened to launch the app.

	     It lives in a real Info.plist rather than an INFOPLIST_KEY_* build
	     setting because that prefix is a DECLARED ALLOW-LIST: Xcode silently
	     drops keys it does not recognise, so INFOPLIST_KEY_GMFSRoot builds
	     cleanly and produces a bundle with no such key — the app then falls
	     through to ~/gmfs and writes PRODUCTION while believing it is isolated.
	     Verified empirically, not assumed.

	     GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE stays YES; Xcode merges the generated keys into
	     this file, so LSUIElement and friends are still managed as build
	     settings. -->
	<key>GMFSRoot</key>
	<string>$(GM_FS_ROOT_BAKED)</string>
	<!-- FOR DISPLAY ONLY. Nothing resolves a path from this. A label that can
	     disagree with the root would be a second source of truth, which is the
	     exact failure the baked root exists to remove. -->
	<key>GMEnvironment</key>
	<string>$(GM_ENV)</string>
	<!-- THE DEV PLUGIN TREE a non-production pane loads with
	     `claude --plugin-dir`, or empty on production.

	     GMDevPluginDir is a REAL key here, not INFOPLIST_KEY_GMDevPluginDir,
	     for exactly the reason recorded against GMFSRoot above: the
	     INFOPLIST_KEY_* prefix is a DECLARED ALLOW-LIST, Xcode silently drops
	     keys it does not recognise, and the result is a bundle with NO key, a
	     build that reports success, and a silent fall-through to "no plugin
	     dir". Verified empirically for GMFSRoot; it would repeat here verbatim.

	     The plugin directory is a property of the BITS, the same kind of fact
	     as the root, so it rides the mechanism this repo already won the
	     argument for rather than a new one.

	     THE KEY IS PRESENT IN ALL THREE CONFIGURATIONS, because the plist is
	     shared. Where GM_DEV_PLUGIN_DIR is unset the variable expands to the
	     EMPTY STRING and the key exists with no value — which is why the
	     reader's `!raw.isEmpty` guard is mandatory, mirroring Paths.swift:77. -->
	<key>GMDevPluginDir</key>
	<string>$(GM_DEV_PLUGIN_DIR)</string>
</dict>
</plist>
